<figure class="execution-flow paper-surface" aria-labelledby="execution-flow-title">
  <figcaption id="execution-flow-title"><strong>Comparing the two plans</strong><br />The plans from our example, showing how many rows each operation handles.</figcaption>
  <div class="routes">
    <section aria-label="Plan for one customer">
      <h3>Customer 42</h3>
      <div class="stage"><strong>Find 10 orders</strong><span>Bitmap index scan → table rows</span></div>
      <p class="flow-arrow">10 order IDs ↓</p>
      <div class="stage join"><strong>10 line lookups</strong><span>Nested loop · 3 lines per order</span></div>
      <p class="flow-arrow">30 joined rows ↓</p>
      <div class="stage"><strong>Sort by product ID</strong><span>Put each product’s lines together</span></div>
      <p class="flow-arrow">30 sorted rows ↓</p>
      <div class="stage aggregate"><strong>Add the quantities</strong><span>GroupAggregate · 3 totals</span></div>
      <p class="flow-arrow">3 totals ↓</p>
      <div class="stage"><strong>Sort by units sold</strong><span>Product 3: 30 · 2: 20 · 1: 10</span></div>
    </section>
    <section aria-label="Plan for all customers">
      <h3>All 1,000 customers</h3>
      <div class="stage"><strong>Read 10,000 orders</strong><span>Build a hash table by order ID</span></div>
      <p class="flow-arrow">Hash table of 10,000 order IDs ↓</p>
      <div class="stage join"><strong>Read 30,000 lines</strong><span>Hash join · probe with each order ID</span></div>
      <p class="flow-arrow">30,000 joined rows ↓</p>
      <div class="stage aggregate"><strong>Add quantities by product</strong><span>HashAggregate · one entry per product</span></div>
      <p class="flow-arrow">3 totals ↓</p>
      <div class="stage"><strong>Sort by units sold</strong><span>Product 3: 30,000 · 2: 20,000 · 1: 10,000</span></div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p class="flow-note">The report for all customers reads each table once. For customer 42, PostgreSQL fetches ten orders and looks up the lines for each one. The counts show rows processed; they do not tell us how long either plan took.</p>
</figure>
